ref 17592186045417] [17592186120057 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120057 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120057 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9bad4bff-0bb7-5ce9-89c2-cbdc3bbadd77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120736 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120736 #edb/ref 1061 19977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120736 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "df182889-cfbe-5906-abbc-45fc241177c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120736 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120737 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120737 #edb/ref 1061 19978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120737 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd1734a2-5193-5182-9a6f-4a024ee32ce5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120737 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120738 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120738 #edb/ref 1061 19980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120738 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8cc42d44-bd5b-5eb5-9e55-ef7a7d93c31a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120738 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120739 #edb/ref 1061 19981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120739 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c27d4e1c-92bf-502f-9c02-c0bf68357dbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120739 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120761 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120761 #edb/ref 1061 25259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120761 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1383e230-aa34-5f36-a91f-c60846be8cc4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120761 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121058 #edb/ref 1064 "The dimension of the column space of a matrix $A$ is called the **rank of $A$**. It's usually denoted by $\\textrm{rank}(A)$. So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Col}(A)).\n$$\n\nFor example, to find the rank of \n![](images/b9/b91bd53b8f1807be516e2477b37fbcd9c3a7415d6cf848d84aa085bc510b5eb4.svg)\nwe write $A$ in row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that there are $2$ pivot columns, namely, the $1$st and the $2$nd. This implies that the first and the second columns of $A$ form a basis of $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ and, therefore, the dimension of $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is equal to $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121058 #edb/ref 1065 3519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121058 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6318f9cd-930b-5b7b-acc7-c27b5b241825" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121058 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121068 #edb/ref 1064 "Note that the number of pivot columns always coincides with the number of non-zero rows in the corresponding row echelon form matrix.\nSo, technically, \n\n$\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of *pivot columns* in the corresponding row echelon form matrix of $A$.\n\nOr, equivalently,\n\n$\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of *non-zero rows* in the corresponding row echelon form matrix of $A$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121068 #edb/ref 1065 4151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121068 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c062d466-946c-526b-aba8-0a0895671218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121068 #edb/ref 1067 "An Alternative Definition of the Rank" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186425010 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425010 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425010 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14c4ed15-45f5-58b1-8360-553b48f39d3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425015 #edb/ref 1080 "A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -5 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425015 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425015 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3832d573-dc8a-5fff-8a6f-0ff08e4abb46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425016 #edb/ref 1080 "D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425016 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425016 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3e5b22e8-a843-5061-9e8c-a7ec0e374b26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425017 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425017 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425017 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f6df2aa-3a3c-5b79-95be-3aa1251322e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425021 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425021 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425021 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50ede2f9-25a2-5752-be09-6a03468fd702" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425027 #edb/ref 1080 "B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425027 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425027 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "711cd429-416c-5181-843f-682cf70b3ece" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425035 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425035 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425035 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3662759-0a3a-5444-ae02-4e604c768bf6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425037 #edb/ref 1080 "C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425037 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425037 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bca51055-1f1e-5521-bd01-c39592fb5371" #edb/r